| `gate evidence record` | `make verify` writes `.evidence/verify.json`: the commit, a dirty flag and a digest of what git lists, each goal's result and exit code, pytest's own test counts and every check's findings. A goal with no junit report, such as `trace`, `eval` or `test-fe`, is listed with its result and `tests: null`. Canonical JSON with no clock, host, user or absolute path, so a rerun on the same tree writes the same bytes; a failing goal, zero tests or a crashed writer leaves it red and the gate failing. | `make verify` | [`evidence.dir`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`evidence.schema`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`JUNIT_XML`](settings.md#make-variables) | No history: one file per gate, replaced on every run. Under `-j` the goals still run in sequence. Where git is not installed or there is no repository its commit is null; a git that ran and failed stops the gate with exit 2. Not an attestation: it is unsigned. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
